{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781550684979,"sessionID":"ses_1334ec25dffedJxBi9Erg6ELZ6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_yPEzkY0g5MSwZfyZplruVGhw","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+## Checkpoint 1: Policy Selection\n+\n+- Controlling policy source: `current_policy.md`\n+- Policy date: `2026-04-20`\n+- Trip dates being audited: `2026-05-08` to `2026-05-10`\n+- Why this policy controls: the current policy is effective for trips starting on or after `2026-05-01`, this trip started on `2026-05-08`, and the current policy explicitly says it supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n+\n+## Rules Applied\n+\n+- Receipt threshold: receipts are required for every expense of `$75.00` or more.\n+- Seat-upgrade rule: seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence.\n+- Lodging cap calculation basis: lodging is capped at `$220.00` per covered night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. Covered nights: `2`, so the maximum reimbursable lodging amount is `2 x $220.00 = $440.00`.\n+- Meal and alcohol rule: meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to `$65.00` per day, and alcohol must be removed from meal receipts.\n+- Ride-share tip cap: ride-share tips are reimbursable up to `20%` of the base fare; any tip above that is non-reimbursable.\n+- Supplies receipt rule: work supplies can be reimbursed only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n+\n+## Stale Policy Note\n+\n+- `stale_policy_excerpt.md` is older (`2026-03-01`) and explicitly warns that it may be stale if a newer policy applies.\n+- Because the current policy applies to this trip and states that it supersedes older excerpts, the stale excerpt does not control this audit.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n+## Checkpoint 2: Item-Level Audit\n+\n+| Expense ID | Claimed Amount | Approved Amount | Non-Reimbursable Amount | Status | Reason |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare with receipt is reimbursable under the current air travel policy. |\n+| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Seat upgrade is not reimbursable because no written preapproval was included in the receipt evidence. |\n+| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Lodging receipt is present, but reimbursement is capped at 2 covered nights x $220.00 = $440.00. |\n+| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Meal receipt is present and required at this amount. Food subtotal of $58.00 is within the daily meal cap; $18.00 of wine is alcohol and not reimbursable. |\n+| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Ride-share base fare of $50.00 is reimbursable. Tip is capped at 20% of base fare, so only $10.00 of the $20.00 tip is reimbursable. |\n+| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Supplies expense is $75.00 or more, so a receipt is required. No receipt was provided, so it is not reimbursable even though the business purpose note is clear. |\n+| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Meal receipt is present and the breakfast amount is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n+## Checkpoint 3: Reimbursement Summary\n+\n+- Reimbursable total: `$1,056.00`\n+- Non-reimbursable total: `$225.00`\n+\n+## Arithmetic\n+\n+- Reimbursable total calculation:\n+  - `T-001 $480.00`\n+  - `T-002 $0.00`\n+  - `T-003 $440.00`\n+  - `T-004 $58.00`\n+  - `T-005 $60.00`\n+  - `T-006 $0.00`\n+  - `T-007 $18.00`\n+  - Total: `$480.00 + $0.00 + $440.00 + $58.00 + $60.00 + $0.00 + $18.00 = $1,056.00`\n+\n+## Decision Buckets\n+\n+- Fully approved expense IDs: `T-001`, `T-007`\n+- Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs: `T-003`, `T-004`, `T-005`\n+- Rejected expense IDs: `T-002`, `T-006`\n+\n+## Finance Note\n+\n+- Current policy controls because the trip began after `2026-05-01`.\n+- Largest reductions came from the lodging cap, alcohol exclusion on the dinner receipt, the ride-share tip cap, the non-reimbursable seat upgrade, and the missing receipt for supplies.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@\n+## Checkpoint 1: Policy Selection\n+\n+- Controlling policy source: `current_policy.md`\n+- Policy date: `2026-04-20`\n+- Trip dates being audited: `2026-05-08` to `2026-05-10`\n+- Why this policy controls: the current policy is effective for trips starting on or after `2026-05-01`, this trip started on `2026-05-08`, and the current policy explicitly says it supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n+\n+## Rules Applied\n+\n+- Receipt threshold: receipts are required for every expense of `$75.00` or more.\n+- Seat-upgrade rule: seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence.\n+- Lodging cap calculation basis: lodging is capped at `$220.00` per covered night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees. Covered nights: `2`, so the maximum reimbursable lodging amount is `2 x $220.00 = $440.00`.\n+- Meal and alcohol rule: meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to `$65.00` per day, and alcohol must be removed from meal receipts.\n+- Ride-share tip cap: ride-share tips are reimbursable up to `20%` of the base fare; any tip above that is non-reimbursable.\n+- Supplies receipt rule: work supplies can be reimbursed only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n+\n+## Stale Policy Note\n+\n+- `stale_policy_excerpt.md` is older (`2026-03-01`) and explicitly warns that it may be stale if a newer policy applies.\n+- Because the current policy applies to this trip and states that it supersedes older excerpts, the stale excerpt does not control this audit.\n\nIndex: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+## Checkpoint 2: Item-Level Audit\n+\n+| Expense ID | Claimed Amount | Approved Amount | Non-Reimbursable Amount | Status | Reason |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare with receipt is reimbursable under the current air travel policy. |\n+| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Seat upgrade is not reimbursable because no written preapproval was included in the receipt evidence. |\n+| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Lodging receipt is present, but reimbursement is capped at 2 covered nights x $220.00 = $440.00. |\n+| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Meal receipt is present and required at this amount. Food subtotal of $58.00 is within the daily meal cap; $18.00 of wine is alcohol and not reimbursable. |\n+| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Ride-share base fare of $50.00 is reimbursable. Tip is capped at 20% of base fare, so only $10.00 of the $20.00 tip is reimbursable. |\n+| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Supplies expense is $75.00 or more, so a receipt is required. No receipt was provided, so it is not reimbursable even though the business purpose note is clear. |\n+| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Meal receipt is present and the breakfast amount is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n\nIndex: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+## Checkpoint 3: Reimbursement Summary\n+\n+- Reimbursable total: `$1,056.00`\n+- Non-reimbursable total: `$225.00`\n+\n+## Arithmetic\n+\n+- Reimbursable total calculation:\n+  - `T-001 $480.00`\n+  - `T-002 $0.00`\n+  - `T-003 $440.00`\n+  - `T-004 $58.00`\n+  - `T-005 $60.00`\n+  - `T-006 $0.00`\n+  - `T-007 $18.00`\n+  - Total: `$480.00 + $0.00 + $440.00 + $58.00 + $60.00 + $0.00 + $18.00 = $1,056.00`\n+\n+## Decision Buckets\n+\n+- Fully approved expense IDs: `T-001`, `T-007`\n+- Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs: `T-003`, `T-004`, `T-005`\n+- Rejected expense IDs: `T-002`, `T-006`\n+\n+## Finance Note\n+\n+- Current policy controls because the trip began after `2026-05-01`.\n+- Largest reductions came from the lodging cap, alcohol exclusion on the dinner receipt, the ride-share tip cap, the non-reimbursable seat upgrade, and the missing receipt for supplies.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md","relativePath":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/an