s that it supersedes older excerpts, the stale excerpt does not control this audit.\n","additions":20,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md","relativePath":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+## Checkpoint 2: Item-Level Audit\n+\n+| Expense ID | Claimed Amount | Approved Amount | Non-Reimbursable Amount | Status | Reason |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare with receipt is reimbursable under the current air travel policy. |\n+| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Seat upgrade is not reimbursable because no written preapproval was included in the receipt evidence. |\n+| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Lodging receipt is present, but reimbursement is capped at 2 covered nights x $220.00 = $440.00. |\n+| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Meal receipt is present and required at this amount. Food subtotal of $58.00 is within the daily meal cap; $18.00 of wine is alcohol and not reimbursable. |\n+| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Ride-share base fare of $50.00 is reimbursable. Tip is capped at 20% of base fare, so only $10.00 of the $20.00 tip is reimbursable. |\n+| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Supplies expense is $75.00 or more, so a receipt is required. No receipt was provided, so it is not reimbursable even though the business purpose note is clear. |\n+| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Meal receipt is present and the breakfast amount is within the $65.00 daily meal cap. |\n","additions":11,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md","relativePath":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\n+## Checkpoint 3: Reimbursement Summary\n+\n+- Reimbursable total: `$1,056.00`\n+- Non-reimbursable total: `$225.00`\n+\n+## Arithmetic\n+\n+- Reimbursable total calculation:\n+  - `T-001 $480.00`\n+  - `T-002 $0.00`\n+  - `T-003 $440.00`\n+  - `T-004 $58.00`\n+  - `T-005 $60.00`\n+  - `T-006 $0.00`\n+  - `T-007 $18.00`\n+  - Total: `$480.00 + $0.00 + $440.00 + $58.00 + $60.00 + $0.00 + $18.00 = $1,056.00`\n+\n+## Decision Buckets\n+\n+- Fully approved expense IDs: `T-001`, `T-007`\n+- Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs: `T-003`, `T-004`, `T-005`\n+- Rejected expense IDs: `T-002`, `T-006`\n+\n+## Finance Note\n+\n+- Current policy controls because the trip began after `2026-05-01`.\n+- Largest reductions came from the lodging cap, alcohol exclusion on the dinner receipt, the ride-share tip cap, the non-reimbursable seat upgrade, and the missing receipt for supplies.\n","additions":27,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md","time":{"start":1781550684952,"end":1781550684976}},"metadata":{"ope